                    "# New York Prison Guard Union Requests Urgent Meeting With State  \nPrison guard strike fallout continues across New York as the union for correction officers has requested an urgent meeting with state officials to address problems like low staffing levels and unsafe work conditions.  \nLast week, the New York State Correctional Officers and Police Benevolent Association (NYSCOPBA) announced that they have requested an urgent meeting with the New York State Department of Corrections and Community Supervision (DOCCS) to discuss two important issues.\n### New York Prison Guard Union Wants Meeting  \nThe union that represents prison guards in New York is hoping to sit down with the agency that runs prisons and oversees inmates as soon as possible to address ongoing issues, according to [News 10](https://www.news10.com/news/ny-news/new-york-prison-guard-union-wants-urgent-meeting-with-doccs-over-staffing-early-release/?utm_medium=social&utm_source=facebook_WTEN&fbclid=IwY2xjawJgiglleHRuA2FlbQIxMQABHrvdyalhAvXZ304KFJ7bXL56ww_yBcpRw1d2PnvV-kXSrZUQ1rnYl16ED88h_aem_3JLOv6-I0TwCLXtQMyccvQ). The union requested the meeting on Friday to address low staffing levels, unsafe work conditions, and to express its concerns over the state's plan to grant an early release to thousands of incarcerated individuals, which some say will worsen public safety.  \nDOCCS Commissioner Daniel Martuscello confirmed the [early release program](https://hudsonvalleycountry.com/new-york-state-releasing-inmates-early/), saying that eligible inmates must meet specific criteria for early release, including that they must be within 15 to 110 days of their approved release date, not serving a sentence for any high-level felonies, violent felonies, or sex offenses, and must have approved housing.\n### SEE ALSO: [Walkout to Honor Police Detective in East Fishkill, New York](https://hudsonvalleycountry.com/walkout-honors-police-detective-east-fishkill-new-york/)  \nThe union has requested that all fired officers be reinstated.",
